<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<odoo noupdate="1">

    <record id="channel_membership" model="slide.channel">
        <field name="name">Membership Management</field>
        <field name="channel_type">training</field>
        <field name="description" type="html">
            <p>Running the club's membership side - dues, the Club app,
            evacuation zones, and the reports that come with it.</p>
        </field>
        <field name="visibility">members</field>
        <field name="enroll">invite</field>
        <field name="is_published" eval="True" />
        <field name="enroll_group_ids" eval="[(6, 0, [ref('membership.group_membership_manager')])]" />
    </record>

    <!-- ============= Section 1: Dues and the Club app ============= -->
    <record id="section_dues" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_membership" />
        <field name="name">Dues and the Club app</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">10</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_dues" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_membership" />
        <field name="name">The Annual Dues product and yearly proration</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">11</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>The suite ships an <strong>Annual Club Dues</strong> product
            with proration turned on and dated to the current calendar
            year - a member who joins mid-year is charged the prorated
            fraction automatically. A daily job
            (<code>_cron_roll_membership_year</code>) moves any prorated,
            expired membership product into the new year on or after
            January 1st, so proration keeps charging new members the right
            fraction every January without anyone editing dates by hand.
            A plain, non-prorated membership product is left alone by this
            job.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_club_app" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_membership" />
        <field name="name">The Club app and its menus</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">12</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>One <strong>Club</strong> app menu gathers Members, Events,
            Volunteers, Equipment Loans, Reporting, and Configuration in
            one place - a front door on top of the Membership, Events, and
            Maintenance apps, which stay installed and reachable on their
            own too. Members also get their own view: signed-in members
            land on <strong>/my/club</strong>, a portal home showing dues
            status, licence class and expiry (with a "Renew soon" badge
            inside the warning window), evacuation zone, equipment
            currently checked out, and upcoming volunteer commitments -
            everything in one glance instead of hunting through several
            apps.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ================ Section 2: Evacuation zones ================ -->
    <record id="section_zones" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_membership" />
        <field name="name">Evacuation zones</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">20</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_zones" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_membership" />
        <field name="name">Evacuation zones</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">21</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>Manage zones under <strong>Club &gt; Configuration &gt;
            Evacuation Zones</strong> - a name, a short code used on
            rosters and net lists, and a zone coordinator (the member who
            leads check-ins for that zone). Assign a member to one from the
            <strong>Evacuation Zone</strong> field on their Membership
            page. A zone's member count updates automatically as people
            are assigned, and zone codes have to be unique so a roster
            never has two zones that look the same.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- =================== Section 3: Reporting =================== -->
    <record id="section_reporting" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_membership" />
        <field name="name">Reporting</field>
        <field name="is_category" eval="True" />
        <field name="sequence">30</field>
    </record>

    <record id="lesson_reporting" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_membership" />
        <field name="name">Member Roster, Event Statistics &amp; Volunteer Participation</field>
        <field name="slide_category">article</field>
        <field name="sequence">31</field>
        <field name="html_content" type="html">
            <p>Under <strong>Club &gt; Reporting</strong>: the
            <strong>Member Roster</strong> lists members with call sign,
            licence class and expiry, membership status and renewal date,
            evacuation zone, and contact details - filter and group by any
            of those (grouped by zone by default), and
            <strong>Print &gt; Member Roster</strong> turns whatever's
            filtered or selected into a PDF. <strong>Event
            Statistics</strong> analyzes one event at a time - attendees,
            volunteers signed up versus slots needed, unfilled slots, and
            understaffed roles - as a graph, pivot, or list.
            <strong>Volunteer Participation</strong> pivots confirmed
            volunteer assignments across every event, by member (who
            actually turns out) or by role (what's hard to fill).
            <strong>Members Analysis</strong> is the OCA membership
            module's own built-in membership/revenue report.</p>
        </field>
    </record>

    <!-- ========================= Quiz ========================= -->
    <record id="slide_quiz" model="slide.slide">
        <field name="channel_id" ref="channel_membership" />
        <field name="name">Check your understanding</field>
        <field name="slide_category">quiz</field>
        <field name="sequence">90</field>
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q1" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="question">A member joins in October. What happens to their Annual Club Dues charge?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">They pay the full year's dues regardless of join date</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">It's automatically prorated for the months remaining</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">They wait until January to be charged anything</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q1_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q1" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">Someone has to manually calculate and enter the prorated amount</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q2" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="question">What keeps the dues product charging the right amount every January without anyone editing dates?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">A daily job that rolls expired prorated products into the new year</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">The treasurer updates it by hand every January</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">It never needs updating once created</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q2_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q2" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">Members request a new product each year</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q3" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="question">Where does a member see their own dues status, licence expiry, and gear on loan?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">/my/club</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">The Member Roster report</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">They have to call the club</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q3_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q3" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">The evacuation zone page</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

    <record id="quiz_q4" model="slide.question">
        <field name="slide_id" ref="slide_quiz" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="question">Which report shows volunteers signed up versus slots needed for one event?</field>
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a1" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">1</field>
        <field name="text_value">Member Roster</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a2" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">2</field>
        <field name="text_value">Event Statistics</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="True" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a3" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">3</field>
        <field name="text_value">Members Analysis</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>
    <record id="quiz_q4_a4" model="slide.answer">
        <field name="question_id" ref="quiz_q4" />
        <field name="sequence">4</field>
        <field name="text_value">Volunteer Participation</field>
        <field name="is_correct" eval="False" />
    </record>

</odoo>
